[{:name "combine-Schwarz-rigidity-with-power-series-uniqueness"
  :lane :solve-lane
  :level :strategy
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:problem-class
   "Show that every coefficient above the linear term vanishes when a pointwise-summable disk power series defines a disk self-map tangent to the identity."
   :coefficient-series
   ["Set `c n = a (n+2)`."
    "Encode `c` as `p = FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars ℂ c`."
    "For every positive real radius `r < 1`, divide the assumed summable shifted series by `r²`."
    "Summability makes the scaled coefficient terms tend to zero; apply `p.le_radius_of_tendsto` and then `ENNReal.le_of_forall_nnreal_lt` to prove `1 ≤ p.radius`."]
   :analytic-construction
   ["Use `p.hasFPowerSeriesOnBall` to obtain differentiability of `p.sum` on the unit disk."
    "Prove `z² * p.sum z = ∑' n, a (n+2) * z^(n+2)` with `FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars_sum_eq`, `tsum_mul_left`, and `pow_add`."
    "Define `f z = z + z² * p.sum z`."
    "The hypotheses make `f` a differentiable disk self-map fixing zero; the product rule gives `deriv f 0 = 1`."
    "Apply the equality case of Schwarz's lemma, here packaged as the local `disk_selfmap_deriv_one_eq_identity`, to obtain `f = id` on the disk."]
   :coefficient-uniqueness
   ["Away from zero, `z² * p.sum z = 0` implies `p.sum z = 0`."
    "At zero, compare the punctured-neighbourhood zero limit with continuity of `p.sum` to fill the removable value."
    "Turn local eventual equality to zero into `p = 0` with `HasFPowerSeriesAt.eq_zero_of_eventually`."
    "Use `FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars_series_eq_zero` and undo the index shift to conclude `a n = 0` for every `n ≥ 2`."]
   :key-api
   ["FormalMultilinearSeries.le_radius_of_tendsto"
    "FormalMultilinearSeries.hasFPowerSeriesOnBall"
    "FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars_sum_eq"
    "HasFPowerSeriesAt.eq_zero_of_eventually"
    "FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars_series_eq_zero"]
   :hypothesis-audit
   "The proof uses the stated `Summable` hypothesis only to obtain termwise convergence after scaling. It does not replace it with absolute summability."
   :witness
   {:declaration "disk_selfmap_tangent_identity"
    :statement-integrity :intact
    :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"]
    :sorryAx false}
   :rule
   "For a disk self-map expressed as identity plus a higher-order series, turn pointwise summability into a convergence-radius bound, use Schwarz rigidity to kill the summed tail, fill its value at the center by continuity, and invoke formal power-series uniqueness to kill its coefficients."
